WEBVTT

00:10:29.541 --> 00:10:34.046
Our ancestors for millennia have been
learning how to use local resources

00:10:34.046 --> 00:10:36.715
to do things like, you know, build tools

00:10:36.715 --> 00:10:37.800
and grow food

00:10:37.800 --> 00:10:39.051
and generate energy.

00:10:39.885 --> 00:10:41.261
So, I mean, we’re lucky.

00:10:41.553 --> 00:10:43.972
We live on a pretty cushy
planet right now.

00:10:44.098 --> 00:10:45.641
That’s why we’re all here today:

00:10:45.641 --> 00:10:47.184
we have everything that we need.

00:10:47.518 --> 00:10:49.019
But Mars is different.

00:10:49.687 --> 00:10:51.522
And Mars is unforgiving.

00:10:52.231 --> 00:10:54.149
And if you run out of food

00:10:54.149 --> 00:10:55.401
or fuel

00:10:55.401 --> 00:10:56.985
or oxygen,

00:10:56.985 --> 00:10:57.986
you’re done.

00:10:58.278 --> 00:11:01.949
So we have to be very smart
about how we do ISRU on Mars.